      {
        "id": 254554,
        "name": "Chief Lackey Rich",
        "username": "Chief_Lackey_Rich",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/6de8d8/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2023-10-14T17:20:02.926Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"fjur\" data-post=\"21\" data-topic=\"30277\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/fjur/48/4849_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> fjur:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Yeah, it’s kind of an outlier with the Materials, as it seems pretty energetic to me. Plus it’s the only Material that was a damage type in <em>SotM</em>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It’s also weirdly broad and has some overlap with Nuclear, given that you can manipulate radioactive waste with it.  Usually find myself limiting what types of Toxic stuff a given character can work with to fit their concept better.  <a href=\"https://villainyunpublished.blogspot.com/2022/08/midas-mini-maxed-metallic-master-minion.html\">Midas here</a> can deal with virtually anything, while <a href=\"https://villainyunpublished.blogspot.com/2022/08/krude-disgusting-mess.html\">Krude</a> specializes in petroleum byproducts with a sideline in industrial waste and <a href=\"https://villainyunpublished.blogspot.com/2023/04/king-blaze-pyromaniacal-lunatic.html\">King Blaze</a> can’t do much with anything but smoke (which is pretty bad for you no matter what’s burning and can be seriously toxic with the right/wrong fuel).</p>",
